	(text "PS/2 KEYBOARD (ATmega328P), KEY LATCH (7802) AND -EF, STATUS (7804)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fa61633b-ca4f-539f-8a5e-bc8d453faa32"))
	(text "The ATmega loads IC9 with LDDATA, which also sets KEY-READY (IC24B); a read of 7802 clears it at TPB (IC20C, IC19B).\nKEY-READY also pulls a bus flag line low through IC23D: JP3 KBD FLAG picks -EF1, -EF2, -EF3 or -EF (set to -EF: EF3\nthrough CPU Rev A's JP1). The VIDEO-G HBIOS polls KEY-READY at 7804, so either CPU card will do. The bus -RESET resets the ATmega through IC18B and IC23E/F. Status (IC8, read\nat 7804): KEY-READY, MOUSE-READY, VSYNC, DE, MONITOR (JP1), GFX-PRESENT, ID 10." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e536e675-334c-5bf6-8eee-668aa32e5cd4"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
